{"name":"Toy Tank Green","hex":"#6d6f4f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Topoiyo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something to play with, especially as intended for use by a child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A thing of little importance or value; a trifle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toy"},{"term":"tank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closed container for liquids or gases.","An open container or pool for storing water or other liquids."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toy","blocks":[{"text":"A toy or plaything is an object that is used primarily to provide entertainment. Simple examples include toy blocks, board games, and dolls. Toys are often designed for use by children, although many are designed specifically for adults and pets. Toys can provide utilitarian benefits, including physical exercise, cultural awareness, or academic education. Additionally, utilitarian objects, especially those which are no longer needed for their original purpose, can be used as toys. Examples include children building a fort with empty cereal boxes and tissue paper spools, or a toddler playing with a broken TV remote. The term \"toy\" can also be used to refer to utilitarian objects purchased for enjoyment rather than need, or for expensive necessities for which a large fraction of the cost represents its ability to provide enjoyment to the owner, such as luxury cars, high-end motorcycles, gaming computers, and flagship smartphones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg/330px-Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy"},{"title":"Tank","blocks":[{"text":"A tank is an armoured fighting vehicle intended as a primary offensive weapon in front-line ground combat. Tank designs are a balance of heavy firepower, strong armour, and battlefield mobility provided by tracks and a powerful engine; their main armament is often mounted within a turret. They are a mainstay of modern 20th and 21st century ground forces and a key part of combined arms combat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Mark_I_series_tank.jpg/330px-Mark_I_series_tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tank"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/500px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/1280px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/500px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Little horse on wheels, Ancient Greek children's toy. From a tomb dating 950–900 BCE, Kerameikos Archaeological Museum, Athens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittle_horse_on_wheels_(Ancient_greek_child's_Toy).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg/250px-Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg/250px-Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy with a hoop. Hoops have long been a popular toy across a variety of cultures.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/